{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeBoundedGenerators","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeBoundedGenerators","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeStableScalarCascade"],"declarations":21,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.stdTwoBelow3_jm_content","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.stdTwoBelow3_jm_content","kind":"theorem","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedGenerators.lean#L172-L194","doc":"**The Jucys–Murphy spectral half, first instance.**\n\nOn the 2-dimensional `(2,1)` representation of `H₃(q)`, the JM elements act on the seminormal\nvector `e₀` by `q^{2c}` for `c = 0, 1, −1` — the contents of the cells `(0,0), (0,1), (1,0)`, i.e.\nof the standard tableau `[[1,2],[3]]`.\n\nThis is the statement `HeckeJucysMurphyElements.lean` records as untouched for want of Young's\nseminormal form.  It is one tableau at one `n`, so it does **not** prove the general spectral\ntheorem; it shows the content spectrum is realised on a genuinely multi-dimensional module. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.stdTwo_jm2_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.stdTwo_jm2_smul","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedGenerators.lean#L163-L170","doc":"`L₂ = σ₁σ₀²σ₁` acts on `e₀` by `q⁻²`, the content-`−1` eigenvalue. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.stdTwo_jm1_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.stdTwo_jm1_smul","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedGenerators.lean#L155-L161","doc":"`L₁ = σ₀²` acts on `e₀` by `q²`, the content-`+1` eigenvalue. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.seminormalE0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.seminormalE0","kind":"def","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedGenerators.lean#L152-L153","doc":"The seminormal vector `e₀ = (1,0)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.stdTwoBelow3_jmRaw_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.stdTwoBelow3_jmRaw_two","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedGenerators.lean#L145-L148","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.stdTwoBelow3_jmRaw_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.stdTwoBelow3_jmRaw_one","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedGenerators.lean#L140-L143","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.stdTwoBelow3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.stdTwoBelow3","kind":"def","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedGenerators.lean#L121-L138","doc":"**The `dim > 1` instance.**  At `n = 3` the bounded presentation asks for exactly two\nHecke-quadratic generators and one braid relation — all three already proved for the Young\nseminormal pair.  Far-commutation is vacuous: it would need `i + 1 < j` with `j + 1 < 3`.\n\nThis is precisely what `HeckeGenerators` cannot admit (`stdTwo_no_stable_extension`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.stdTwoσ_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.stdTwoσ_one","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedGenerators.lean#L119-L119","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.stdTwoσ_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.stdTwoσ_zero","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedGenerators.lean#L118-L118","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.stdTwoσ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.stdTwoσ","kind":"def","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedGenerators.lean#L112-L116","doc":"The generator family: `σ₀ = stdTwo0`, and every later index `stdTwo1`.  Only `σ₀` and `σ₁` are\nconstrained at `n = 3`, so the tail is free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRawB_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRawB_succ","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedGenerators.lean#L103-L104","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRawB_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRawB_zero","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedGenerators.lean#L101-L101","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRawB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRawB","kind":"def","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedGenerators.lean#L95-L99","doc":"**Unnormalized JM elements** on the bounded presentation: `L₀ = 1`, `L_{i+1} = σᵢ Lᵢ σᵢ`.\nSame recursion as `jmRaw`; `jmRawB H k` for `k < n` touches only `σ₀ … σ_{k-1}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.HeckeGeneratorsBelow.far","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.HeckeGeneratorsBelow.far","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedGenerators.lean#L91-L91","doc":"**Far commutation**, whenever both indices are generators of `H_n(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.HeckeGeneratorsBelow.braid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.HeckeGeneratorsBelow.braid","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedGenerators.lean#L89-L89","doc":"**Braid relation**, whenever both `σ i` and `σ (i+1)` are generators of `H_n(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.HeckeGeneratorsBelow.hecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.HeckeGeneratorsBelow.hecke","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedGenerators.lean#L87-L87","doc":"**Hecke relation**, for each generator of `H_n(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.HeckeGeneratorsBelow.σ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.HeckeGeneratorsBelow.σ","kind":"def","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedGenerators.lean#L85-L85","doc":"The braid generators; only `σ i` for `i + 1 < n` is constrained. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.HeckeGeneratorsBelow.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.HeckeGeneratorsBelow.mk","kind":"ctor","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedGenerators.lean#L82-L82","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.HeckeGeneratorsBelow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.HeckeGeneratorsBelow","kind":"class","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedGenerators.lean#L74-L91","doc":"**Bounded Hecke presentation.**  The relations of `H_n(q)`, required only for the generator\nindices that actually occur there: `σ₀ … σ_{n-2}`, i.e. `i + 1 < n`.\n\nContrast `HeckeGenerators`, which quantifies over every `i : ℕ` and so presents `H_∞(q)`.  That\ndifference is not cosmetic — `stdTwo_no_stable_extension` shows the unbounded version excludes the\n2-dimensional representation outright.\n\nNo `σinv` field: §1 derives the inverse from `hecke`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.sub_mul_hecke_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.sub_mul_hecke_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedGenerators.lean#L66-L70","doc":"The other side: `(X − (q − q⁻¹)) · X = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.hecke_mul_sub_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.hecke_mul_sub_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedGenerators.lean#L59-L64","doc":"`X · (X − (q − q⁻¹)) = 1` for any Hecke-quadratic `X`.  Scalars are central, so this is pure\nrearrangement — no invertibility hypothesis is needed. ","signatureChunk":0}]}